      <h2 class="section__title">Branding and Design Costs</h2>
      <p class="section__text">
        Branding and design costs range from $200 to $5,000 depending on complexity and professional level. DIY branding costs $200-500 for logo design using Canva or similar tools. Professional branding costs $1,000-3,000 for logo, brand guidelines, and initial marketing materials. Comprehensive branding costs $3,000-5,000 for full brand identity including packaging design, social media templates, and website graphics.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Logo design costs $50-500. DIY using Canva costs $0 but requires design skills. Freelance designers on Fiverr charge $50-200 for logo design. Professional design agencies charge $500-2,000. Start with a freelance designer for cost-effective professional results. Ensure your logo works in color and black-and-white, and scales for different applications.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Brand guidelines cost $200-1,000. Brand guidelines specify logo usage, color palette, typography, and voice. DIY brand guidelines using free templates cost $200-500. Professional brand guidelines cost $500-1,000. Brand guidelines ensure consistency across all touchpoints and are essential as your brand grows.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Packaging design costs $100-1,000. Basic packaging with logo sticker costs $100-300. Custom packaging design costs $500-1,000. Custom packaging enhances unboxing experience and brand perception but adds unit cost. Start with basic packaging and upgrade to custom as revenue grows. SDF Clothing can apply your branding to packaging during production.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Photography costs $500-3,000 for initial product and lifestyle images. DIY photography with a smartphone costs $0 but requires skill. Professional product photography costs $20-50 per image. Lifestyle photography costs $500-2,000 per shoot. High-quality images are essential for e-commerce conversion - invest in professional photography as budget allows.
      </p>
