      <p class="section__text">
        Legal and administrative costs range from $200 to $3,000. Business formation costs $50-500 depending on structure and location. Trademark registration costs $225-400 per class plus attorney fees if using legal counsel. Contracts and agreements cost $200-1,000 for terms of service, privacy policy, and wholesale agreements. Insurance costs $300-1,000 annually for general liability and product liability coverage.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Business formation costs vary by structure. Sole proprietorship costs $50-150. LLC costs $100-500. Corporation costs $200-1,000. Consult with a tax professional to choose the right structure for your situation. LLC is the most common choice for clothing brands due to liability protection and tax flexibility.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Trademark registration costs $225-400 per class with the USPTO. Clothing brands typically register in Class 25 (clothing). Consider registering your brand name and logo separately. DIY trademark registration is possible but complex - consider an attorney for valuable brands. International trademark registration costs $1,000-5,000 per country if expanding globally.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Contracts and agreements cost $200-1,000. Essential documents include terms of service, privacy policy, refund policy, and wholesale agreements. Use templates from legal service providers like LegalZoom or Rocket Lawyer for cost savings. Have an attorney review custom agreements for wholesale partnerships.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Insurance costs $300-1,000 annually. General liability insurance covers third-party claims. Product liability insurance covers product-related claims. Business interruption insurance covers lost income from disasters. Insurance is essential for protecting your business from lawsuits and claims. Our <a href="/how-to-start-a-clothing-brand">starting guide</a> includes legal checklists for clothing brands.
