      <div class="faq">
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">How much does it cost to start a clothing brand?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Clothing brand startup costs range from $5,000 to $50,000 depending on scale and approach. Minimal approach: $5,000-10,000 (basic website, 3-5 styles, minimal marketing). Moderate approach: $10,000-25,000 (professional website, 5-8 styles, e-commerce setup, launch marketing). Comprehensive approach: $25,000-50,000 (full e-commerce, 8-12 styles, professional branding, substantial marketing). Production costs represent 40-60% of total startup budget. SDF Clothing offers low MOQ manufacturing starting at 300 pieces, reducing initial inventory investment.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What are the biggest startup costs for a clothing brand?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            The biggest startup costs are production/inventory (40-60% of budget), marketing (15-25%), website/e-commerce (5-15%), branding/design (5-10%), legal/administration (3-5%), and operations/shipping (3-5%). Production costs are the largest expense because you must pay upfront for inventory before selling. Marketing is the second-largest expense, essential for customer acquisition. Website and e-commerce setup is necessary for direct-to-consumer sales. Branding and design establish brand identity. Legal costs include trademark registration and business formation.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">How do I minimize startup costs for my clothing brand?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Minimize startup costs by starting with fewer styles (3-5 instead of 8-12), using low MOQ manufacturing (300 pieces instead of 1,000), launching with a simple website (Shopify basic plan instead of custom), doing marketing yourself initially (social media instead of paid ads), using print-on-demand for initial sales instead of holding inventory, and focusing on one sales channel (e-commerce instead of wholesale + retail). SDF Clothing's low MOQ manufacturing enables starting with minimal inventory investment while maintaining professional quality.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">How much should I budget for production costs?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Budget $3,000-15,000 for production costs depending on scale. At 300 pieces per style at $10-15 per unit, 3 styles cost $9,000-13,500. At 500 pieces per style, 3 styles cost $15,000-22,500. Production costs include fabric, labor, trims, and shipping. Fabric represents 40-50% of unit cost, labor 30-40%, trims 10-15%, shipping 5-10%. Payment terms are typically 30% deposit and 70% before shipment. SDF Clothing provides transparent cost breakdowns and flexible payment terms to manage cash flow.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">How much does marketing cost for a clothing brand launch?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Marketing costs for clothing brand launch range from $1,000 to $15,000 depending on approach. Minimal: $1,000-3,000 (social media content, organic reach, influencer barter). Moderate: $3,000-8,000 (paid social ads, micro-influencers, email marketing setup). Comprehensive: $8,000-15,000 (major influencer campaigns, paid search, PR outreach, content production). Customer acquisition cost varies by channel - Instagram $5-20 per customer, Facebook $8-25, Google Shopping $10-30, Influencers $15-40. Start with organic and low-cost channels, scale to paid as revenue grows.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">What are the ongoing costs after launching a clothing brand?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Ongoing costs after launch include production/inventory (variable cost per unit), marketing (10-20% of revenue), website/e-commerce ($30-300/month), shipping/fulfillment ($3-8 per order), payment processing (2.9% + $0.30 per transaction), and operations/administration (5-10% of revenue). Production costs increase with sales volume - budget 40-50% of revenue for ongoing production. Marketing should scale with revenue - start at 10% and increase to 20% as you optimize. SDF Clothing supports ongoing production with volume pricing as you scale.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">How much should I budget for website and e-commerce?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Budget $500-5,000 for website and e-commerce setup. Basic Shopify: $500-1,000 (Shopify basic plan $29/month, free theme, minimal apps). Professional Shopify: $1,000-3,000 (Shopify plan $79/month, premium theme $200-500, essential apps $200-500, custom design $500-1,500). Custom website: $3,000-10,000 (custom development, advanced functionality, integrations). Start with Shopify basic plan for minimal upfront cost, upgrade as revenue grows. E-commerce is essential for direct-to-consumer sales and customer data collection.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq__item">
          <h3 class="faq__question">How do I calculate my break-even point?</h3>
          <p class="faq__answer">
            Calculate break-even by dividing fixed startup costs by gross margin per unit. If startup costs are $15,000 and gross margin per unit is $25, break-even is 600 units sold. Fixed costs include website setup, branding, legal, and initial marketing. Variable costs per unit include production cost, shipping, payment processing. Gross margin = retail price - variable costs. Track actual costs against projections to refine your break-even calculation. Most clothing brands reach break-even within 6-18 months depending on marketing effectiveness and product-market fit.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
